# Swiftacular Swift patch manifest — the single source of truth for which patches
# apply.sh applies, shared by the VM/Ansible flow and the Kubernetes image build.
#
# One patch per row.  Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Columns (whitespace-separated):
#
#   patch_file   path of the .patch file, relative to this directory
#   level        the -p<level> strip count passed to patch(1)
#   target_subdir  directory the patch applies in, relative to the Swift package
#                  root (each OS prepends its own root, e.g. the deb dist-packages
#                  path or the CentOS site-packages path)
#
# To add a future patch: drop the .patch file here and add one row below.
# No change to apply.sh, the Dockerfiles, or the playbooks is required.
#
# patch_file        level  target_subdir
2_sharder.patch     0      container
